# Guitar Tuner — .plan

## Session 5 & 6 — Professional-Grade Android Tuner & Complete Audio Pipeline Fix

### Root Causes of "No Sound / No Recognition"

#### 1. CRITICAL: Android AudioRecord HAL float32 Unsupported
- In `useAudioStream`, `encoding: 'float32'` requested `AudioFormat.ENCODING_PCM_FLOAT`.
- Android Audio HAL on physical devices / emulators fails `AudioRecord.getMinBufferSize` with `ERROR_BAD_VALUE` (-2) for `ENCODING_PCM_FLOAT`, throwing `AudioStreamUnsupportedConfigException` on `stream.start()`.
- Fix: Switched native audio capture to `encoding: 'int16'` (`AudioFormat.ENCODING_PCM_16BIT`), which is universally supported on 100% of Android devices. Converted incoming 16-bit PCM integer samples to normalized `Float32Array` in [-1.0, 1.0].

#### 2. CRITICAL: TunerScreen Did Not Auto-Start Listening
- `TunerScreen` lacked an auto-start `useEffect`. Upon launching the app, microphone stream remained inactive (`idle`) until manually pressed.
- Fix: Added automatic listening lifecycle on mount with clean release on unmount in `TunerScreen.tsx`.

#### 3. CRITICAL: Hanning Window Distorting YIN Time-Domain Autocorrelation
- Multiplying the time-domain signal by a Hanning window caused $x[i] - x[i+\tau]$ to have non-zero envelope discrepancy $(win[i] - win[i+\tau] \ne 0)$.
- This inflated CMNDF at the fundamental period above the 0.10 threshold (e.g. Low E2 minimum CMNDF was ~0.15, failing the detector).
- Fix: Removed Hanning window from time-domain difference function. YIN difference function must run on unwindowed samples with constant integration window $W = N - \tau_{max}$.

#### 4. CRITICAL: Stale Frame Age Gate & 15ms Rate Limiter
- Android delivers audio buffers in ~100ms intervals.
- The previous 60ms stale frame age gate dropped every buffer after the first.
- Fix: Removed frame age gate and rate limiter, allowing the native audio stream to dictate buffer delivery naturally.

#### 5. CRITICAL: StabilityFilter Threshold Mismatch
- StabilityFilter default confidence threshold blocked valid note passes.
- Fix: Tuned `confidenceThreshold = 0.20` in `useTuner.ts` and set default `0.6` in `StabilityFilter` to satisfy unit test contracts.

#### 6. CLEANUP: Android-Only Specialization
- User requested Android only and removal of iOS directory.
- Removed `apps/mobile/ios` directory.
- Removed iOS configuration blocks from `apps/mobile/app.json`.
- Removed `ios` script from `apps/mobile/package.json`.
- Removed iOS-specific `setAudioModeAsync` code paths from `useTuner.ts`.

## Session 7 — Complete Emoji Removal & Vector Icon Standardization

### Goal
Replace all unicode emojis and symbols (`🔒`, `⚡`, `✓`, `↑`, `↓`, `♭`, `♯`, `›`) across the app with vector icons (`Feather` from `@expo/vector-icons`).

### Changes
1. **TunerScreen.tsx**:
   - Replaced `🔒 LOCKED` badge with `<Feather name="lock" size={11} color={theme.colors.accent} />` and clean bold text `LOCKED`.
   - Replaced `Tap string to lock-on ›` hint with clean text and `<Feather name="chevron-right" size={10} color={theme.colors.accent} />`.
2. **ErrorBoundary.tsx**:
   - Replaced lightning emoji `⚡` with `<Feather name="zap" size={28} color="#D97706" />`.
3. **TunerStateBanner.tsx**:
   - Removed emoji arrows and checkmarks (`✓`, `↑`, `↓`) embedded in text labels.
   - Preserved Feather icons (`check-circle`, `arrow-up`, `arrow-down`, `chevron-up`, `chevron-down`, `target`) rendered next to labels.
4. **CentsGauge.tsx**:
   - Replaced `♭ FLAT` and `SHARP ♯` unicode text with `<Feather name="trending-down" size={11} /> FLAT` and `SHARP <Feather name="trending-up" size={11} />`.

